WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.955
Here is the core idea.

00:00:04.035 --> 00:00:07.989
Take a mixture with unconstrained real weights,

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:12.024
so components can have negative coefficients, and
simply square the whole thing.

00:00:12.104 --> 00:00:16.058
Squaring forces the output to be non-negative no
matter what the weights are.

00:00:16.138 --> 00:00:20.093
Expanding the square turns a K-component mixture
into a sum over all pairs of components,

00:00:20.173 --> 00:00:24.127
a product-of-experts form whose partition function
can still be computed in closed form for many families.

00:00:24.207 --> 00:00:28.162
To go deep,

00:00:28.242 --> 00:00:32.196
the authors square a tensorized
structured-decomposable circuit layer by layer.

00:00:32.276 --> 00:00:36.231
Each squared layer holds a quadratic number of
units but still outputs a vector,

00:00:36.311 --> 00:00:40.265
so the whole model trains efficiently with gradient
descent,

00:00:40.345 --> 00:00:44.300
computing the normalizer just once per batch.
